          "id": "1780650962136",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779098547563_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Inputs**\n1. LedgerList: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.ledgers}}\n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Oracle Fusion ledger selection, You must adhere to the standard `oraInfoDisplay` Knowledge Base.\n\n**DIRECTIVE**\nTransform `LedgerList` into one valid `oraInfoDisplay` block using the `multiRecordWidget`.\n\n**ROOT CONFIGURATION**\n- Do not include a root title.\n- Do not include a root description.\n- Do not include a summary.\n- Use `multiRecordWidget`.\n\n**DISPLAY RULES**\n- Each ledger object contains `ledgerName` and `ledgerId`.\n- Preserve the input order from `LedgerList`.\n- Do not display `ledgerId`.\n- Do not invent, infer, or add ledger values.\n- If `LedgerList` is empty, missing, null, or not an array, render the `multiRecordWidget` with no rows.\n\n**COLUMN RULES**\nCreate exactly these columns in this order:\n1. `Ledger Name`\n   - Display the exact `ledgerName` value.\n\n**ACTION LOGIC**\nEvery row must include an action for the `Select` button.\n\nUse this command:\n\n`ora.Invoke(\"selectLedger\", {\n  \"command\": \"selectLedger\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"ledgerName\": \"{ledgerName}\",\n    \"periodName\": \"{Period}\"\n  }\n})`\n\nAction payload rules:\n- Pass the exact ledger name from the current row.\n- Pass the exact `Period` input value.\n- Do not pass `ledgerId`.\n- Do not pass the full ledger object.\n- Do not add any extra payload keys.\n- The action context must be valid JSON with double quotes.\n\n**OUTPUT RULES**\n- Output only the final `oraInfoDisplay` block.\n- Do not output explanations or instructional text.\n- Do not add title, description, summary, or extra fields.\n- Do not include markdown."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6821.75,
            "y": 7426
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract User Search Intent",
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780915649647"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_USER_SEARCH_INTENT",
          "id": "1780655628823",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780655628823_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "input_message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nYou are a filter extractor for Ledger Insights.\n\nYour only output category is searchInsights.\n\nExtract searchable filters from input_message when they are directly present or\nclearly implied by the user input.\n\nSearchable filters:\n- status\n- category\n- priority\n- ruleName\n\nSupported status values:\n- Open\n- Reviewed\n- Dismissed\n- Obsolete\n\nSupported status typo normalization:\n- obselete -> Obsolete\n\nSupported priority values:\n- High\n- Medium\n- Low\n\nCategories are free-form.\nThe category does not need to match any predefined list.\nExtract category values directly from the user input when they are used as\nfilters for insight records.\nDo not invent category values.\n\nExamples:\n- show insights\n- get insights\n- list insights\n- find insights\n- show open insights\n- show reviewed variance insights\n- display high priority insights\n- get dismissed intercompany insights\n- search insights with rule name \"Unusual Balance\"\n- show insights for rule Cash Variance\n- list obsolete low priority period end controls insights\n- find insights where status is open and priority is high\n- show accounting controls with status reviewed\n- get clearing and accrual insights\n- search process exceptions insights\n- show insights by rule name \"Intercompany Out of Balance\"\n- filter obselete variance insights\n- view ledger insights\n- open ledger insights\n\nDo not answer the user's question.\nDo not explain insights.\nDo not provide recommendations.\nDo not answer unrelated substance.\nOnly extract filters and return the required JSON object.\n\nStatus extraction:\n- Extract status only when the user explicitly mentions one of the supported\n  statuses or a supported status typo.\n- Normalize supported status typos to the supported status value.\n- Preserve the status text as entered by the user except for supported typo\n  normalization.\n\nPriority extraction:\n- Extract priority only when the user explicitly mentions one of the supported\n  priorities.\n- Preserve the priority text as entered by the user.\n\nCategory extraction:\n- Extract category when the user provides a category-like phrase for filtering\n  insights.\n- The category does not need to match any predefined list.\n- Preserve the category text as entered by the user.\n- Category values may be single words or multi-word phrases.\n- Do not invent category values.\n- Do not treat status, priority, or rule name values as category.\n- Do not treat search verbs as category.\n- Do not treat the word \"insights\" as category.\n\nRule name extraction:\n- Extract ruleName when the user mentions \"rule\", \"rule name\", \"named\", or\n  provides a quoted rule-like phrase.\n- Preserve the ruleName text as entered by the user, except remove surrounding\n  quotes.\n- Do not treat category, status, or priority words as ruleName.\n\nOutput rules:\n\nOutput only valid JSON in this exact shape:\n\n{\n  \"code\": \"searchInsights\",\n  \"filters\": {\n    \"status\": [],\n    \"category\": [],\n    \"priority\": [],\n    \"ruleName\": []\n  }\n}\n\nRules:\n- code must be exactly searchInsights\n- always include filters\n- filters.status must contain only extracted status values\n- filters.priority must contain only extracted priority values\n- filters.category must contain only category values extracted from the user\n  input\n- filters.ruleName must contain only extracted rule names\n- if no filters are extracted, return searchInsights with all four filter\n  arrays empty\n- if multiple values are present for one filter, include all values\n- do not include explanations, markdown, or extra text\n- do not include any root-level key other than code and filters\n- do not output value\n- do not output values\n- do not output filter\n- do not output arrays outside the filters object"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"code\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"value\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"code\",\n    \"value\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5019.5,
            "y": 6982
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Payload for User Query",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const normalizeText = (value) => {\n  return String(value ?? \"\")\n    .trim()\n    .toLowerCase();\n};\n\nconst buildOrLikeFilter = (field, values = [], shouldNormalize = true) => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(values) || !values.length) return \"\";\n\n  const validValues = values\n    .map(value =>\n      shouldNormalize\n        ? normalizeText(value)\n        : String(value ?? \"\").trim()\n    )\n    .filter(Boolean);\n\n  if (!validValues.length) return \"\";\n\n  return `(${validValues\n    .map(value => `${field} ~like '%${value}%'`)\n    .join(\" OR \")})`;\n};\n\nconst buildCategoryCodeLookupMap = () => {\n  const categoryCodeLookup = $context.$variables.OraGLRuleCategory ?? [];\n\n  const categoryMap = new Map();\n\n  categoryCodeLookup.forEach((item) => {\n    const code = item?.value;\n    const label = item?.label;\n\n    if (!code) return;\n\n    if (label) {\n      categoryMap.set(normalizeText(label), code);\n    }\n\n    categoryMap.set(normalizeText(code), code);\n  });\n\n  return categoryMap;\n};\n\nconst mapCategoriesToCodes = (categories = []) => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(categories) || !categories.length) return [];\n\n  const categoryMap = buildCategoryCodeLookupMap();\n\n  return categories\n    .map(category => categoryMap.get(normalizeText(category)))\n    .filter(Boolean);\n};\n\nconst buildLedgerInsightsQuery = ({\n  status = [],\n  categories = [],\n  priority = [],\n  ruleNames = []\n} = {}) => {\n  const mappedCategoryCodes = mapCategoriesToCodes(categories);\n\n  const categoryFilter = buildOrLikeFilter(\n    \"sensorSignal.policy.categoryCode\",\n    mappedCategoryCodes,\n    false\n  );\n\n  const statusFilter = buildOrLikeFilter(\n    \"status.meaning\",\n    status\n  );\n\n  const priorityFilter = buildOrLikeFilter(\n    \"sensorSignal.policy.rulePriority.meaning\",\n    priority\n  );\n\n  const ruleNameFilter = buildOrLikeFilter(\n    \"sensorSignal.policy.ruleName\",\n    ruleNames\n  );\n\n  const activeFilter = \"sensorSignal.policy.activeFlag=true\";\n\n  const ledgerId =\n    $context.$nodes.PROCESS_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.ledgerId;\n\n /* const ledgerFilter =\n    `sensorSignal.sensorInsightDetails[dataAccessSetAssignment.ledgerId=${ledgerId}]`;*/\n\n  const filters = [\n    categoryFilter,\n //   ledgerFilter,\n    activeFilter,\n    statusFilter,\n    priorityFilter,\n    ruleNameFilter\n  ].filter(Boolean);\n\n  return [\n    `$filter=${filters.join(\" AND \")}`,\n    `$sortBy=sensorSignal.policy.rulePriority.lookupCode:asc,timeCreated:desc`,\n    `sensorCode=LedgerInsights`\n  ].join(\"&\");\n};\n\nconst intent = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_USER_SEARCH_INTENT?.$output;\n\nconst searchFilters = intent?.filters ?? {};\n\nlet statusFilter = searchFilters.status ?? [];\nlet categoryFilter = searchFilters.category ?? [];\nlet priorityFilter = searchFilters.priority ?? [];\nlet ruleNameFilter = searchFilters.ruleName ?? [];\n\nconst mappedCategoryCodes = mapCategoriesToCodes(categoryFilter);\n\n\nconst hasNoFilters =\n  statusFilter.length === 0 &&\n  categoryFilter.length === 0 &&\n  priorityFilter.length === 0 &&\n  ruleNameFilter.length === 0;\n\nconst hasOnlyUnmappedCategoryIntent =\n  statusFilter.length === 0 &&\n  categoryFilter.length > 0 &&\n  mappedCategoryCodes.length === 0 &&\n  priorityFilter.length === 0 &&\n  ruleNameFilter.length === 0;\n\n\n\nif (hasNoFilters || hasOnlyUnmappedCategoryIntent) {\n  let inpMsg = $context.$system.$inputMessage ?? \"\";\n  const enteredQuery = inpMsg.trim();\n\n  if (enteredQuery) {\n    ruleNameFilter.push(enteredQuery);\n  }\n}\n\n// Default status to Open only when the user did not provide status\nif (statusFilter.length === 0) {\n  statusFilter.push(\"Open\");\n}\n\nconst query = buildLedgerInsightsQuery({\n  status: statusFilter,\n  categories: categoryFilter,\n  priority: priorityFilter,\n  ruleNames: ruleNameFilter\n});\n\nreturn query;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780916554634"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_PAYLOAD_FOR_USER_QUERY",
          "id": "1780915649647",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5000,
            "y": 7204
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Subtitle",
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_SUBTITLE",
          "id": "1780909915449",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780909915449_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Ledger Operations text rendering assistant.\n\nUse only these inputs:\nledgerName = {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.ledgerName}}\nperiodName = {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.periodName}}\nendDate = {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.endDate}}\ncurrentDate = {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nCalculate `daysDifference` as the integer day difference:\n`endDate - currentDate`\n\nFormat the status text as follows:\n\n- If `$daysDifference = 1`, return `Day - 1`\n- If `$daysDifference > 1`, return `Day - {daysDifference}`\n- If `$daysDifference = 0`, return `Day - 0`\n- If `$daysDifference = -1`, return `1 day after close`\n- If `$daysDifference < -1`, return `{absolute value of daysDifference} days after close`\n\nReturn only one plain-text line in this exact order:\n{periodName}    {daysToClose}\n\nSpacing rule:\n- Between values, use exactly four literal Unicode non-breaking space\n  characters: U+00A0 U+00A0 U+00A0 U+00A0.\n- Do not use normal spaces for the separators."
            }
          ],
